cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PurffleShorts in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "PurffleShorts: open-source AI YouTube Shorts generator and upload autopilot"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chaman Raj
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chamanrajragu/purffle-shorts"
url: "https://purffle.com/purffle-shorts/"
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
keywords:
  - youtube shorts generator
  - ai video generator
  - text to video
  - faceless video
  - llm
  - text to speech
  - ffmpeg
  - model context protocol
abstract: >-
  PurffleShorts turns a topic, web page, document or long video into finished vertical Shorts:
  an LLM of your choice writes and self-reviews the script, free neural voices narrate it,
  stock footage or AI images illustrate each sentence, word-synced captions are burned in with
  ffmpeg, and the result is uploaded or scheduled on YouTube.
